3. Sigstore's TUF root: roots/sigstore_tuf_root.json

The root metadata of Sigstore's TUF repository (https://github.com/sigstore/root-signing), which src/tuf.rs
builds in: Apache License, Version 2.0.


4. Test data (tests/data/; the tests read it, the library does not contain it)

- tests/data/wycheproof/: Project Wycheproof test vectors (https://github.com/C2SP/wycheproof), Apache License,
  Version 2.0. See the README there.
- tests/data/sigstore/: the npm packages sigstore 0.2.0, 2.2.0 and 4.0.0 (sigstore-js) with their attestations,
  the pypi-attestations 0.0.30 wheel with its provenance, and Sigstore's trusted root as sigstore-python embeds
  it: Apache License, Version 2.0, each package with its own LICENSE inside. See the README there.
- tests/data/ed25519_sign_input.txt: cases from the sign.input of the Ed25519 reference software of Daniel J.
  Bernstein et al. (public domain), as Go's crypto/ed25519 ships it.
- Certificates, CRLs, OCSP responses, transparency-log data and attestations captured from public servers and
  registries (tests/data/real_chains, real_revocation, sumdb, rekor, sigstore): public data. The README or
  header next to each says where and when it was captured.
- Expected results recorded from other implementations (Go, OpenSSL, Python's cryptography and zlib, quic-go,
  ls-qpack, python-h2, hyperframe, aioquic, python-tuf) are their outputs; none of their code is in this
  repository.
